WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.170
Everyone keeps a list of things they want.

2
00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.570
Almost nobody knows what that life
would cost, or when they could have it.

3
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.290
Dandelist turns that list into a plan.

4
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.550
Say or type the first thing you want.

5
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.790
A Muse Spark agent searches the web,
reads the page the price comes from,

6
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.670
and only calls a price checked
when it's printed there.

7
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.270
A real photo follows,
checked for size and subject.

8
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.650
Then a few quick picks, made from your
wish, and when you'd like it all by.

9
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.170
Make an account with a code sent to
your email, and the list is yours.

10
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.090
Come back, and it welcomes you
with one of your own wishes.

11
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.430
Say several wishes at once, and each
gets its own card while you keep talking.

12
00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:03.330
It understands what you mean: a pink
G-Wagon is a Mercedes G-Class in pink.

13
00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:07.450
Name only a brand, and you
pick the model by photo.

14
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.890
Can't remember the name?

15
00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:11.510
It makes a best guess and offers others.

16
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.210
Wish for money, and a
slider asks how much.

17
00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.730
Wish for love, and it stays priceless.

18
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.890
Describe a home or a car,
and the agent opens the right tool:

19
00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.370
real listings to swipe through,
or a car priced from the maker.

20
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.730
When you're done,
it prices the best match.

21
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.910
Here are ten wishes,
arranged however you like.

22
00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:46.370
Ask your Dandy to sort them by price,
and one tap puts them back.

23
00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.890
Each day brings a new pick that
fits what you already want.

24
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.390
Open any wish to see what's
behind it: the checked price

25
00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:59.190
and where it came from,
what it costs to keep,

26
00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.430
with the published rate for every line,

27
00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:03.830
and the options an expert would give you.

28
00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:06.690
Slide the timeline to see
what it takes each month.

29
00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:11.680
Tell Dandy what you meant, and it looks
again, with a photo of the new find.

30
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.110
The plan adds it all up:
what it costs today,

31
00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:23.010
what it costs to keep,
and the income it would take.

32
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.730
Dandy remembers what matters to you.

33
00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.090
Every theme has its own song.

34
00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:35.810
And your own agent can run your list, too.

35
00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:41.870
The agent runs on Meta's Model
API: Muse Spark for the hunt,

36
00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:47.690
Muse Voice Transcribe for what you say,
and SAM and Muse Image for the pictures.

37
00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:52.210
Dandelist.

38
00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:55.250
Price the life you want.
